eonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This thread will run for two weeks, after which we'll perform the fixes for the final PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:54:18-08:00","id":427942,"title":"","content":"Incendax, that is a development change to reflect the fluid nature of spirits. Its intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:05:52-08:00","id":427948,"title":"","content":"Page 94 a header seems missing. Page 93 ends with regeneration and suddenly 94 begins to talk about senses across the gauntlet<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok at looking closer it seems more like Page 94 and 95 have switched places and need to be read so that you read 95 first then 94","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:06:30-08:00","id":427949,"title":"","content":"I think Incendax is more commenting that that's a weird sentence. Is it supposed to read<br /> <br /> &quot;so impressed her many Firstborn children&quot;<br /> <br /> or what? The whole sentence is &quot;Our dedication to Mother Wolf\u2019s duty so impressed her many of her Firstborn children, and they bless our tribes, each dedicated to hunting a specific prey.&quot; That's...rambly and run-on-y and I don't like it. Making my brain hurt.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 272: </b><i>alaghadim </i>is misspelled, either as <i>alaghidim </i>or <i>alaghadim</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:11:02-08:00","id":427952,"title":"","content":"Page 75 side-bar, not sure &quot;Gulls&quot; warrants the capital G.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:12:12-08:00","id":427953,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 274:</b> In &quot;Boles\u0142aw the Wry-Mouthed&quot; there is a box instead of letter &quot;\u0142&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:12:22-08:00","id":427954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=427942#post427942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incendax, that is a development change to reflect the fluid nature of spirits. Its intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>The typo appears to be the double use of the word <b>her</b>, and the way it makes the rest of the sentence read. But it is up to you guys if it is legit or not.<br /> The important thing is bringing anything to your attention, so you can make a decision one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:23:23-08:00","id":427966,"title":"","content":"p. 13: &quot;A furry head forced its way through the <b>hole, more</b> plaster flaked away as a plump body followed.&quot; I feel like there's an <i>and </i>missing there? Or some kind of conjunction.<br /> <br /> p. 13: &quot;She sniffed at the air, eyes still <b>one </b>him...&quot;<br /> <br /> Unrelated: That story is gonna give me freaking nightmares. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:23:34-08:00","id":427968,"title":"","content":"I love new corebook. But the expression &quot;<i>Father Luna</i>&quot; makes my teeth cringe. Could not we have in book just used two versions: &quot;Mother Luna&quot; and &quot;Father Moon&quot;? They are self-explaining, no need for this language monster.<br /> <br /> Location - p.16 onward <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:47:06-08:00","id":428007,"title":"","content":"p. 301: &quot;Successive uses of the Evil Eye on a given character suffer a cumulative User to get an e7240 with extra monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.1 penalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> The words &quot;User to get an e7240 with extra monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.&quot; are a dialect form of saying &quot;minus&quot; and absolutely nothing to do with a rogue copy/paste from my day-job's ticketing system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":28,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","user":"DigitalRaven","date":". 03-04-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:48:51-08:00","id":428010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=427968#post427968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love new corebook. But the expression &quot;<i>Father Luna</i>&quot; makes my teeth cringe. Could not we have in book just used two versions: &quot;Mother Luna&quot; and &quot;Father Moon&quot;? They are self-explaining, no need for this language monster.<br /> <br /> Location - p.16 onward <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. The name for Luna shifts even more than that of Father Wolf and that's deliberate. Sie is of fluid gender, and in some places we quite deliberately refer to hir with a paternal pronoun and feminine name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T12:55:58-08:00","id":428018,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 26.</b> <i>&quot;She can\u2019t change make her Initiative result higher or lower than the target\u2019s if it isn\u2019t already.&quot;</i><br /> Change OR Make might work, instead of change make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:01:09-08:00","id":428023,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 276</b>: &quot;Le&lt;box&gt;nica&quot; should be &quot;Le\u015bnica&quot;. BTW, a question: why some names have Polish diacritics (Boles\u0142aw, Le\u015bnica, Sob\u00f3tka, Ostr\u00f3w Tumski) while others (Wroclaw, Sleza, wilkolaki, poludnica) don't? I'm not saying that the only correct spelling is the one including diacritics (it can be done without them), but it would be good to choose a convention and stick to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:08:24-08:00","id":428031,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 20: </b>&quot;You memorized the Oath of the Moon <b>with </b>a day of your First Change...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:12:29-08:00","id":428035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428023#post428023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Page 276</b>: &quot;Le&lt;box&gt;nica&quot; should be &quot;Le\u015bnica&quot;. BTW, a question: why some names have Polish diacritics (Boles\u0142aw, Le\u015bnica, Sob\u00f3tka, Ostr\u00f3w Tumski) while others (Wroclaw, Sleza, wilkolaki, poludnica) don't? I'm not saying that the only correct spelling is the one including diacritics (it can be done without them), but it would be good to choose a convention and stick to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, I had all the relevant accents etc in the original draft version I wrote, I guess they vanished somewhere during the transition into layout? I haven't got my copy yet so can't check just how many are missing but, for example, it should be Wroc\u0142aw, wilko\u0142aki, Po\u0142udnica etc.<br /> <br /> I guess by using Polish words I apparently broke the layout software <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:31:13-08:00","id":428066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428035#post428035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, I had all the relevant accents etc in the original draft version I wrote, I guess they vanished somewhere during the transition into layout? I haven't got my copy yet so can't check just how many are missing but, for example, it should be Wroc\u0142aw, wilko\u0142aki, Po\u0142udnica etc.<br /> <br /> I guess by using Polish words I apparently broke the layout software <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It appears your \u0142 characters got eaten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:41:05-08:00","id":428082,"title":"","content":"Pages 94 and 95 are transposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:42:23-08:00","id":428083,"title":"","content":"p252 onwards. If Bristol is in the &quot;United Kingdom&quot;, then so is Belfast. Northern Ireland would also be a lot more appropriate than Ireland, which is generally used to refer to the Republic rather than the physical island. While Ireland is technically correct, it made me double take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5233-kathd","name":"KathD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:48:09-08:00","id":428084,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 97.</b> &quot;<b>Rage: A</b> Gauru-form Uratha&quot;<br /> The letter A is accidentally bolded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:59:03-08:00","id":428093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428035#post428035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't got my copy yet so can't check just how many are missing but, for example, it should be Wroc\u0142aw, wilko\u0142aki, Po\u0142udnica etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing Polish words in official setting in Poland - it makes my heart warm! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:02:28-08:00","id":428095,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 16: </b>The subheading under Cahalith says &quot;The Visionary -- <b>The Gibbous Moon</b>&quot;, but it's the only Auspice that follows that pattern. The others lack the moon phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:09:50-08:00","id":428116,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 97: </b>The Gauru doesn't seem to have a species factor on speed, don't know if this is intentional or not.<br /> <b>p. 98: </b>The book doesn't specify what you Clash with during the Clash of Wills when two pre-emption powers are used.<br /> <b>p. 104: </b>The Breaking Point sidebar doesn't have sub-headers for above and below Harmony 8 and Harmony 3.<br /> <b>p. 110: </b>Shouldn't the Warcry merit be resisted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":". 03-04-2015, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:32:02-08:00","id":428130,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 26:</b> &quot;An Irraka can respect the value in having a reputation, but at the end of the day it just means people know who you are and have a place to start looking for advantages \u2014 <b>more than one new-moon has planned a successful hunt based on boasting and reputation</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong grammatically, I'm just not sure that the sentence after the dash follows logically. It seems contradictory. Is there a &quot;<b>but</b>&quot; missing?<br /> <br /> I might just be reading it wrong.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, I see what it means.<b> Ignore me!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-04-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:38:03-08:00","id":428137,"title":"","content":"On page 94.<br /> &quot;The chart below sets out how long she can go without being...&quot;<br /> The chart is above. If the pages are transposed that may be the issue.<br /> <br /> Page 108.<br /> 'With four dots, the attack gains one level of weapon damage atop its normal advantages.'<br /> What's a level of weapon damage? Like one extra lethal? Lethal to aggravated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:55:05-08:00","id":428194,"title":"","content":"* Odd numbered pages have no page numbers on them.<br /> * On page 189, under the Open Condition, it says that Control Influence can upgrade Resonant to Open. It should be Strengthen Influence as per the chart and diagram above.<br /> * Also on page 189, under the Controlled Condition, it should say that the Control Influence can upgrade Open to Controlled under Causing the Condition.<br /> <br /> Note that these latter two problems are also in the God-Machine Chronicle book and should be fixed when the new World of Darkness book comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T15:06:43-08:00","id":428204,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 28: </b>First line of the right hand column: the word &quot;<b>triggered</b>&quot; is obscured by a tree branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T15:13:32-08:00","id":428208,"title":"","content":"While I have the time tonight and tomorrow (before going back to work) I am going to attempt to do a grammar pass through. This will be slow going so no idea how far I will get, but totally worth it to create the best possible book.<br /> <br /> <b>Page 15</b> has an awkward sentence.<br /> Original: Our dedication to Mother Wolf's duty so impressed her many of her Firstborn children, and they bless our tribes, each dedicated to hunting a specific prey.<br /> <br /> My suggested change would be as follows to try and keep the same tone.<br /> <br /> Our dedication to Mother Wolf's duty impressed many of her Firstborn children that they in turn now bless our tribes, each dedicated to hunting a specific prey<br /> <br /> <b>Page 15</b>: Weband should be We Band (1st paragraph upper right)<br /> <b>Page 16</b>: Pyrrhic should be lowercase (upper right top)<br /> <b>Page 16: </b>described should be describe (1st full paragraph right side)<br /> <b>Page 16</b>: awkward sentence in 2nd full paragraph right side.<br /> Original: She welcomes the prey as part of that legend, though.<br /> Suggested change: Cahaliths welcome prey as part of their legend<br /> <br /> <b>Page 16</b>: 3rd full paragraph right side has an incorrect comma placement in sentence<br /> &quot;A Cahalith has to be the living repository for the pack's <b>exploits and, often, her</b> tribe's lore.&quot;<br /> should be changed to<br /> &quot;A Cahalith has to be the living repository for the pack's <b>exploits, and often, her </b>tribe's lore.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Page 16</b>: 3rd full paragraph right side has incorrect period placement<br /> &quot;Not every pack understands that their gibbous-moon might now want to tell their favorite joke for the <b>tenth time. And yet,</b>&quot;<br /> should be changed to<br /> &quot;Not every pack understands that their gibbous-moon might now want to tell their favorite joke for the <b>tenth time, and yet,</b>&quot;<br /> <b>Page 64</b>: world of flesh should have Flesh capitalized for consistence with rest of book (2nd paragraph right side)<br /> <b>Page 143</b>: world of flesh should have Flesh capitalized for consistence with rest of book (top of page left side)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-04-2015, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T15:50:25-08:00","id":428238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428194#post428194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Odd numbered pages have no page numbers on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in the upper-right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T16:08:04-08:00","id":428249,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">page 301 in the evil eye description &quot;Successive uses of the Evil Eye on a given character suffer a cumulative User to get an e7240 with extra monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.1 penalty&quot;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <br /> Hope it helped<br /> <br /> Andy ANTHOINE<br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5235-zarkis","name":"Zarkis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T16:33:54-08:00","id":428289,"title":"","content":"So, the Rapture Numen is not the same as the one in the <i>God-Machine Chronicle/WoD 2e</i> book. In WtF (p. 192), Rapture causes the Stunned Tilt. In the core book, it causes Insensate (and, imo, Insensate makes more sense given that Rapture is like a supernaturally-induced drug trip). Insensate is also not listed in the Tilts section at the back of WtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3236-quantumelody","name":"quantumelody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3236_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T17:10:40-08:00","id":428310,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 11:</b> &quot;WHITE WOLF BOOKS<br /> This book contains everything you need to play Werewolf:<br /> The Forsaken, but over the years we\u2019ve published many other<br /> books for the World of Darkness that can enhance your game<b>.</b>&quot;<br /> Missing dot at the end of the sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T17:11:56-08:00","id":428313,"title":"","content":"p.96: 'The Hishu form is more human than human&quot;' missing quotation marks before 'more'<br /> p.97: &quot;The Gauru form only communicates, to help with the kill.&quot; The comma makes this read as &quot;The only thing the Gauru form does is communicate. Doing this helps with the kill.&quot; Without the comma it would read (I believe correctly) &quot;The Gauru form only communicates if this would help with the kill&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T17:59:38-08:00","id":428360,"title":"","content":"<b>Pages 96-98</b><br /> <br /> Many of the forms have the following statement in some form<br /> &quot;Bite attacks can establish grapples as well as cause damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that if I attack someone in Urhan form for example, I can not only inflict damage on my target, but also place them in a grapple as well in the same turn? Or should it instead be read as they can choose to inflict damage OR establish a grapple?<br /> <br /> This is difficult to understand since every form uses slightly different wording.<br /> <br /> <b>Gauru</b><br /> Bite and claw attacks can establish grapples in addition to causing damage (implies that it can do both in the same turn due to grammar)<br /> <br /> <b>Urshul</b><br /> Bite attacks can establish grapples as well as cause damage (implies that when using a bite attack, you can deal damage and grapple in same turn)<br /> <br /> <b>Urhan</b><br /> Bite attacks attacks deal +1 lethal damage and do not require a grapple. They can establish a grapple as well as cause damage (implies either damage + grapple in same turn, or select which attack to use)<br /> <br /> I feel this section needs to be made significantly more clear in the final product especially due to the different verbiage used. Some may read this as that simply means the forms are allowed to make grapple attacks while in those forms, while others may interpret it as double attacks of damage + grapple.<br /> <br /> <b>Page 103</b><br /> There is also confusion over Kuruth triggers as listed in another thread where the text could possibly be cleaned up. Posting it here as well<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428707-confusion-over-triggers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-over-triggers</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-05-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T19:22:05-08:00","id":428433,"title":"","content":"p. 93: On the Primal Urge chart, it lists &quot;<i>Basu-Im</i> Time&quot; for each level of PU, with the time <u>increasing</u> as PU goes up. The fluff text, however, describes that time as going <u>down</u> as PU rises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T20:05:31-08:00","id":428465,"title":"","content":"page 26, under Connections for Rahu, &quot;To the Irraka, the kill is quick, silent, and sure. because the kill the goal.&quot; There seems to be an is missing between &quot;the kill&quot; and &quot;the goal.&quot; May have been overlooked because there is a line break right where the is should go.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Further down the same page, under the auspice benefit <i>closer than you thought</i>, first bullet point. &quot;She can't change make her Initiative result higher or lower than the target's if it isn't already.&quot; I'm guessing it should either just be &quot;can't make her initiative&quot; or &quot;can't change <i>to</i> make her initiative&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2015, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T20:19:27-08:00","id":428473,"title":"","content":"Page 97. Gauru. Rage. <br /> &quot;If an opponent is out of each...&quot; Should be &quot;If an opponent is out of reach...&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, any reason for the auspice phases out of order? It seems a bit... Odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/735-hitashippo","name":"HitAShippo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:13:40-08:00","id":428608,"title":"","content":"On the actual character sheet PDF, under the Gauru section it has Initiative (+1) ___. Ok so far, but right underneath Teeth/Claws; it goes on to say (Initiative +3). Does that overwrite the first derived value or is only in certain cases like Death Rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T21:39:23-08:00","id":428659,"title":"","content":"Page 135: &quot;This Facet affects all or part of a single structure, or an area of up to the Uratha\u2019s <b>Cunning</b> Renown x 10 yards in radius.&quot; This is for the Glory Facet.<br /> <br /> Page 137: &quot;The Uratha achieves an exceptional success on Perception rolls with <b>3</b> successes instead of <b>5.</b>&quot; For the sake of consistency with similar effects in the same book, these numbers should probably be spelled out as words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-05-2015, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:17:47-08:00","id":428740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428608#post428608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the actual character sheet PDF, under the Gauru section it has Initiative (+1) ___. Ok so far, but right underneath Teeth/Claws; it goes on to say (Initiative +3). Does that overwrite the first derived value or is only in certain cases like Death Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the initiative modifier for those weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:30:44-08:00","id":428746,"title":"","content":"Character Creation, p. 83, Initiative is stated as Dexterity+Wits, but other books are Dexterity+Composure.<br /> <br /> Also it's not listed in the Advantages paragraph on the Quick Reference p. 84.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","user":"amaterasu","date":". 03-05-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:31:20-08:00","id":428747,"title":"","content":"p83: &quot;Initiative is your character\u2019s Dexterity + Wits.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is either a rules change, a modification for the werewolf template, or an error. If it's one of the first two that's not clearly explained anywhere. It should be Dexterity + Composure.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually! I just went and checked all of the statblocks in the book, because it's a slow night I guess, and all but two of them line up with Dexterity + Composure. So I figure it was an error, meaning so are these:<br /> <br /> Funnel Web statblock (p204) - Initiative should be 7.<br /> <br /> Information Broker statblock (p207) - Initiative should be 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:34:58-08:00","id":428748,"title":"","content":"p192: &quot;If the victim fails a Resolve + Primal Urge roll, she gains a <b>temporary derangement</b> for the spirit\u2019s Power in days, in a form that binds her closer to the spirit\u2019s wishes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should say condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:39:23-08:00","id":428749,"title":"","content":"p. 84, Experience Cost chart:<br /> <br /> Affinity Gif","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T23:49:37-08:00","id":428754,"title":"","content":"p. 232, right column, third paragraph down: &quot;...true nature is belied even this terrible imitation...&quot;<br /> <br /> Should probably be &quot;true nature <b>belies </b>even this terrible imitation...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T00:26:36-08:00","id":428799,"title":"","content":"The rules for Speed are not consistent. The Character Creation follows what's stated in Requiem 2nd Edition, of Strength + Dexterity + Size (which conflicts with WOD Core which has a Species Factor, not Size, it's just Humans have both at 5). The inconsistency comes up in the Shapeshifting rules: Dalu and other forms do not take the Size change and factor it into the Speed bonus listed (For Example: Dalu has Strength +1, Stamina +1, Size +1, and lists Health as +2, which is the Stamina+Size bonus, but lists Speed as +1, which is only the Strength bonus, not Strength+Size bonus if we're using Size for Speed). In addition, Urshul and Urhan list Species Speed Factor for their Speed bonuses that go above the Attribute bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Personal preference is keeping Species factor and not including Size in the Speed trait, but that's another discussion thread, I'm sure.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T00:29:06-08:00","id":428803,"title":"","content":"P. 98, &quot;Chase Down&quot; lists the roll for Foot Chase as Strength + Athletics, however the roll is Stamina+Athletics and is listed as such on p. 155 with the rules for Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T00:33:15-08:00","id":428807,"title":"","content":"Possible conflict or confusion: Wolf Senses on p. 95 (should be p. 94 as prior posts note) state Uratha can identify each other with a smell roll, but Hunter's Aspect on p. 98 states they know each other at a glance. And while it could be the one under Wolf Senses is more about recognizing the identity of someone, the write-up under Hunter's Aspect really strongly implies that they fully recognize each other automatically with all their possible senses all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T00:45:09-08:00","id":428817,"title":"","content":"Not exactly errata, but among the PDF 'links' to different sections (which you can pull up with Adobe Reader and such) Edoloth is listed twice under the Ausipice section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T01:46:39-08:00","id":428863,"title":"","content":"p.185: &quot;As noted earlier, spirits use the lower of <b>Finesse or Resistance</b> for Defense unless they are Rank 1, in which case they use the higher.&quot; Should be <b>Power or Finesse</b>.<br /> <br /> p.186: &quot;Spirits in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other spirits <b>of the same type</b>, unless the attack utilizes the spirit\u2019s bane.&quot; Bolded text is carried over from the common Ephemeral Beings rules but confuses matters by its inclusion here.<br /> <br /> p.188: Flowchart should only have &quot;Resonant&quot; in first box below &quot;Conditions on Environment&quot; header. Arrow labeled &quot;Repeated Possession&quot; pointing the wrong way.<br /> <br /> Also, despite the explicit dice bonus to crossing over that compatible spirits receive at a locus, I can't seem to find the dicepool spirits use to cross the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-05-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T03:06:09-08:00","id":428905,"title":"","content":"<b>EDIT: </b>NEVERMIND. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 03-05-2015, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:19:02-08:00","id":428944,"title":"","content":"...I'm not totally sure if this counts as errata, but all of the hotlinks to the Conditions appendix just take me to the first page of the PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:46:44-08:00","id":428991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428799#post428799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for Speed are not consistent. The Character Creation follows what's stated in Requiem 2nd Edition, of Strength + Dexterity + Size (which conflicts with WOD Core which has a Species Factor, not Size, it's just Humans have both at 5). The inconsistency comes up in the Shapeshifting rules: Dalu and other forms do not take the Size change and factor it into the Speed bonus listed (For Example: Dalu has Strength +1, Stamina +1, Size +1, and lists Health as +2, which is the Stamina+Size bonus, but lists Speed as +1, which is only the Strength bonus, not Strength+Size bonus if we're using Size for Speed). In addition, Urshul and Urhan list Species Speed Factor for their Speed bonuses that go above the Attribute bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Personal preference is keeping Species factor and not including Size in the Speed trait, but that's another discussion thread, I'm sure.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Speed is indeed calculated by Strength + Dexterity + Species Factor. Any time it says Size (including in VtR2nd), it's an error. As you said, it keeps cropping up because Size and Species Factor are the same for humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:46:57-08:00","id":428992,"title":"","content":"The Kuruth Triggers section is very unclear. It says each character has her own set of triggers, but doesn't explain how to select them. Do I pick one category (like &quot;moon&quot; or &quot;other&quot;) and take the Common, Specific, and Passive all from the same list? Do I chose one Common, one Specific, and one Passive from any category? Am I only supposed to have one trigger of each level? I can't divine the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:47:17-08:00","id":428993,"title":"","content":"pages 96-97, the Dalu,Urshul and Gauru forms descriptions mentions that they inflict respictivelly mild, moderate and full Lunacy, but in the Lunacy sections there is no mention of different forms of Lunacy, just bonus and penalties and it doesn't mention any bonnus or penalty to Urshul. Also while it explicitely says that Werewolf jaws cause lethal damage as mystical sources, it isn't clear about the claws, the Dalu description went out of this ways to say it causes lethal to humans, the other forms mentions no such thing, leading me to believe they cause mystical damage, it's not clear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:52:54-08:00","id":428998,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is errata, but it would be handy if the Character Creation Quick Reference (p 84) listed the starting rating of Renown and Harmony. That stuff is currently listed at the bottom of the character sheet.<br /> I wasn't able to find the number of Touchstones or Rites a starting character gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 03-05-2015, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:59:11-08:00","id":429001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428998#post428998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is errata, but it would be handy if the Character Creation Quick Reference (p 84) listed the starting rating of Renown and Harmony. That stuff is currently listed at the bottom of the character sheet.<br /> I wasn't able to find the number of Touchstones or Rites a starting character gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Number of Touchstones is listed in the longer character creation rundown (it's two). I don't think it specifies category there, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T11:57:58-08:00","id":429097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=428993#post428993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also while it explicitely says that Werewolf jaws cause lethal damage as mystical sources, it isn't clear about the claws, the Dalu description went out of this ways to say it causes lethal to humans, the other forms mentions no such thing, leading me to believe they cause mystical damage, it's not clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IIRC, Only bites are mystical, but claws do lethal - so beings that don't take lethal damage against non-mystical attacks would downgrade the claws to bashing but not the bite.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you just gotta get your teeth in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:07:59-08:00","id":429121,"title":"","content":"p. 85 -- &quot;<b>she can always pick a Facet of a Wolf Gift to buy with Renown, and each Facet costs two Experiences</b>.&quot; but the chart on p. 84 says that Wolf Gift Facets cost 1 experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:08:02-08:00","id":429122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429097#post429097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> IIRC, Only bites are mystical, but claws do lethal - so beings that don't take lethal damage against non-mystical attacks would downgrade the claws to bashing but not the bite.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you just gotta get your teeth in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could put in a sentence pointing that out-&quot;while a werewolf's claws are ferocious, the teeth are...&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the text for pages 94 and 95 seem to have been switched around. It talks about healing, then suddenly switches to shapeshifting for a page, then it continues on about healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:30:34-08:00","id":429156,"title":"","content":"Not exactly errata, but the character sheet is missing a place for Touchstones. You could put them in other places, but it might make sense for a couple spaces for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:56:05-08:00","id":429270,"title":"","content":"p. 101: &quot;Unless a weapon is forged out of silver, it counts as an improvised weapon (see p. 168).&quot;<br /> <br /> This sentence reads strangely, as though any weapon not forged out of silver would count as improvised. I suggest changing it to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Unless a silver weapon is forged for combat, it counts as an improvised weapon (see p. 168).&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:53:39-08:00","id":429319,"title":"","content":"Is Berserker's Might not being usable in Urshul form intentional? It seems odd to have it work in just Dalu and Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:12:28-08:00","id":429331,"title":"","content":"As others have noted before me, the Kuruth Triggers seem to be poorly explained and the Forms make reference to degrees of Lunacy that aren't included in the book. Those are the two biggest things that stand out to me right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:25:12-08:00","id":429341,"title":"","content":"The actual lunacy rules make it pretty clear that &quot;mild&quot; lunacy gets a +2 bonus on the integrity roll, &quot;moderate&quot; gets no modifier and &quot;full&quot; gets a -2 penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:33:46-08:00","id":429353,"title":"","content":"Page 53 under &quot;Lodge of the Chronicle:&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;By the time the hunt was complete and the battle was won, dozens of werewolves had died, and the lore and history of two generations of Uratha was one.&quot;<br /> <br /> In that sentence &quot;one&quot; should probably be &quot;gone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1517-bluegrassgeek","name":"BluegrassGeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:03:39-08:00","id":429370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429341#post429341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual lunacy rules make it pretty clear that &quot;mild&quot; lunacy gets a +2 bonus on the integrity roll, &quot;moderate&quot; gets no modifier and &quot;full&quot; gets a -2 penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh! Well then... thank you! I must have missed that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:36:15-08:00","id":429453,"title":"","content":"On page 95: &quot;Uratha may use Primal Urge in place of a roll to identify a character she remembers, even if he\u2019s hiding or disguised.&quot;<br /> <br /> What does that mean? It seems to imply you aren't rolling but &quot;use Primal Urge&quot; doesn't really tell you how it works.<br /> <br /> Also, a few more spirit things:<br /> * 1st edition Book of Spirits specified that Conceptual/Abstract spirits had a species factor of 10. This would be good to add in since there is no other guidance on what species factor to use for them, otherwise.<br /> * It should be clarified in the Spirits section that they can cross over at a Locus without needing Gauntlet Breach, as is implied in Chapter 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:55:19-08:00","id":429481,"title":"","content":"p. 59: &quot;Anyway, I saw this woman at the.third party?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:12:05-08:00","id":429490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429341#post429341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual lunacy rules make it pretty clear that &quot;mild&quot; lunacy gets a +2 bonus on the integrity roll, &quot;moderate&quot; gets no modifier and &quot;full&quot; gets a -2 penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be deduced but it isn't clear. It would be best if they scrapped this degrees of Lunacy and streight put the the modifiers in the Forms descripition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:24:25-08:00","id":429548,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is intentional or not, but the effects of extreme Harmony imbalance are given as Harmony 8+ or Harmony 3-. With there being Harmony 0 and Harmony 5 being dead center, it seems like this should be Harmony 2- to make the symmetry complete. This would effect page 100 (under Reaching) and 104 (the Breaking Points chart and also the first paragraph under it, regarding Reaching again).<br /> <br /> 10 Stuck in Flesh<br /> 8-9 no locus needed to Reach to Flesh<br /> 3-7 no special considerations<br /> 1-2 no locus needed to Reach to Shadow<br /> 0 Stuck in Shadow<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Similarly, the Blood and Bone merit seems like it should be for Harmony 3-7, not 3-8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":2019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","user":"eberg","date":". 03-05-2015, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:30:48-08:00","id":429552,"title":"","content":"Several mortal merits seem to be missing, like Multidisciplinary Specialty and Professional Training (unless those were intentionally removed).<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of merits, on the interactive character sheet, all the merits in the dropdown list are 1st edition.<br /> <br /> ...I remember seeing somewhere a comma that should have been a semicolon, but damned if I can find it now. So, uh. Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 03-05-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:48:38-08:00","id":429581,"title":"","content":"The moon taint condition references the sick tilt, which doesn't appear in the appendix at the back. Also i don't see a clear statement of a werewolf doing aggravated damage to spirits of lesser rank, additionally would that apply to a idigam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","user":"pgolasze13","date":". 03-05-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:55:47-08:00","id":429604,"title":"","content":"There is no explanation of how Style merits work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T19:10:22-08:00","id":429622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429604#post429604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no explanation of how Style merits work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T19:51:41-08:00","id":429634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429581#post429581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moon taint condition references the sick tilt, which doesn't appear in the appendix at the back. Also i don't see a clear statement of a werewolf doing aggravated damage to spirits of lesser rank, additionally would that apply to a idigam?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also a couple Dread Powers that reference the Sick Tilt. It needs to be added to the Appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T19:53:19-08:00","id":429635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429622#post429622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several merits marked as Style merits. There is no explanation of what this means. There is a short paragraph in God-Machine that gives the rules for them which needs to be added here, since it is supposed to be a self-contained rule set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:11:25-08:00","id":429669,"title":"","content":"The description of using Hard Leverage under Forcing Doors on page 164 makes references to Humanity. The system, as written, doesn't really work with Harmony, since Harmony breaking points don't have &quot;levels&quot;, so you can't just swap Humanity for Harmony. The rules will need a re-write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:34:55-08:00","id":429701,"title":"","content":"On page 170, under <b>Type</b>, reference is made to &quot;metal club&quot;, which is not a weapon listed on the table. I wager it should be &quot;baton&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:38:29-08:00","id":429851,"title":"","content":"p.128 Lore of the Land facet is missing a dice pool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:39:51-08:00","id":429853,"title":"","content":"Possible contradiction.<br /> <br /> Page 99: &quot;Each time your character increases her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every time she increases a different Renown, she gains a Facet of a Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 115: &quot;Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown, she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she possesses at no cost.&quot;<br /> <br /> Devblogs by Stew led us to believe you get both a free moon facet and a shadow/wolf facet when you raise your auspice renown. If such is still the case, and thus both parts are correct, these two segments should be in the same section of the book and clarified as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T02:27:50-08:00","id":429963,"title":"","content":"On page 85 Wolf Gift Facets are noted as costing 2 experiences, while in the experience chart on page 84 lists them as costing 1.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, someone else already found that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T02:33:19-08:00","id":429964,"title":"","content":"* p95 and p98. Wolf senses, smell and Hunter's Aspect. I'm confused about how identifying werewolves works. Wolf senses says that this is a rolled Instant action, but the start of the Hunter's Aspect section says it's automatic. <br /> * p98 - 100. There are no hyperlinks or page cross-references from the list of hunter's aspects or renown conditions, which makes it quite hard to look up what these do. As a general point, it would be fantastic if every reference to a Condition was hyperlinked to the Appendix (I understand there may not always be space for a page reference, and it's much easier to flick between sections in a physical book).<br /> * p100 - 101. There's inconsistent use of some terminology in the Reaching rules. E.g. the text in Reaching talks about &quot;the spirit world&quot; when the table of modifiers talks about &quot;the shadow&quot;. <br /> * p87. Similarly, the Touchstone rules talk about physical touchstones giving you a bonus to avoiding &quot;harmony loss&quot; rather than &quot;breaking points towards flesh&quot;<br /> * p100 - 101 and p 104. The section on Reaching explains that Harmony 8 / 2 lets you cross the gauntlet without a locus, but not that Harmony 10 / 0 characters cannot cross over. The Harmony section only mentions that Harmony 10 / 0 characters cannot cross over, and doesn't mention than Harmony 8 / 2 can cross without a locus. It would be better to have all of the Harmony/Reaching rules interactions in the same place.<br /> * p204 - The Beshilu artwork covers up text at the bottom of the first column","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5233-kathd","name":"KathD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T03:17:21-08:00","id":429971,"title":"","content":"Page 118 - &quot;The Cahalith adds her Glory Renown <b>to her all</b> dice pools for Expression and Persuasion.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T03:46:48-08:00","id":429996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KathD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=429964#post429964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* p87. Similarly, the Touchstone rules talk about physical touchstones giving you a bonus to avoiding &quot;harmony loss&quot; rather than &quot;breaking points towards flesh&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean &quot;Breaking points towards <i>spirit.</i>&quot; The same passage also calls breaking points toward flesh &quot;breaking points towards humanity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:35:18-08:00","id":430018,"title":"","content":"p. 117 &quot;She perceives everything that the spirit does with perfect clarity, and may spend a point of Essence to apply a penalty equal to her Wisdom Renown<b> to all single Perception rolls </b>that the spirit makes for one scene.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:23:49-08:00","id":430087,"title":"","content":"On page 200, the Ivory Claw has a Pure Bred (Purity) merit which is not referenced elsewhere in the book.<br /> On page 207, the hunter has a Firefight merit which is not referenced elsewhere in the book.<br /> On page 207, the information broker has the Encyclopedic Knowledge and Eye for the Strange merits, which are not referenced elsewhere in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:24:12-08:00","id":430089,"title":"","content":"p. 181 - I think the Animals umia should read Mammals instead, since all the example ilthum are mammals.<br /> <br /> Also on the same page, in the top-right paragraph on Elementals: &quot;or long-lasting than other <i>umia'</i>...&quot; There's an apostrophe just hanging around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:15:08-08:00","id":430164,"title":"","content":"Posting this here per recommendation in another thread ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429937-totem-advantages-questions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ages-questions</a> )<br /> <br /> <b>Are the Advantage(s) granted by a Totem limited to +1 Dot?</b> All of the examples seem to imply yes, but there's nothing explicitly stated. If multiple dots are allowed, does that mean the totem can bring a WW or Wolf-Blooded to 7 or higher? If multiple dots are allowed and traits can not exceed 6 (or PU+1, whichever is higher), what happens?<br /> <br /> <b>Do people gaining a merit as an Advantage need to meet the prerequisites?</b> If yes, and they don't qualify, what happens? If no, how does this work for Merits that simply make no sense for that individual pack member? Anchored for a human character, for instance. If no, does this include granting Supernatural merits to werewolves?<br /> <br /> <b>Can &quot;Totem&quot; merit and &quot;Dedicated Locus&quot; merit be granted by the Totem Merit?</b> As a related question, can a Pack have more than one dedicated locus.<br /> <br /> <b>Do all choices regarding a Merit need to be the same?</b> If a Totem grants Allies or Professional Training, do all choices (subject of the Allies, type and Asset Skills of Professional Training and granted benefits) have to be the same?<br /> <br /> <b>Can Retainers be pack members?</b> If yes, do they gain the Advantages of a totem? If yes, what happens when you select &quot;Retainer&quot; as one of your Totem advantages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:42:37-08:00","id":430205,"title":"","content":"On pages 208-209, there are several references to the Urged being able to use Influences on others. However, the description of the Fettered Condition on page 190 clearly states that the spirit can only use its Influences and numina on the fetter itself. Depending on how this is resolved, the Hate-Monger needs Influences added to his stat block.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":2019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","user":"eberg","date":". 03-06-2015, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:51:42-08:00","id":430212,"title":"","content":"On page 210, the Fire Elemental Dread Power has no Essence cost or duration, unlike the other three Elemental powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:02:28-08:00","id":430221,"title":"","content":"On page 313, the Poisoned Tilt begins with the stray word Personal before the Description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:27:08-08:00","id":430243,"title":"","content":"pg 126: &quot;Scent the Unnatural will not detect Uratha <b>r</b> the use of Gifts...&quot;<br /> pg. 127: Still Small Voice Gift - &quot;This Facet can be used against any number of Uratha in Wasu-Im who can hear the speaker\u2019s words. Targets cannot<br /> <b>choose not to resist even if they sorely desire to indulge the oncoming fury</b>.&quot; This doesn't make sense. The sole purpose of the power is to calm Death Rage. If they choose not to resist the power would make effect immediatly, If someone want to indulge they would chooseto<b> resist</b> the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 03-06-2015, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:41:40-08:00","id":430266,"title":"","content":"I realized this belonged in Errata.<br /> <br /> Page 61 of Werewolf states, under Hishu,<br /> <br /> &quot;Most Uratha are most comfortable in human shape. Others see it as just another tool to use on the hunt. While wearing the Hishu skin, a werewolf hides amongst humanity. Efforts to pick her out of the crowd and identify her as somehow supernatural fail, even if those attempts are supernatural in their own right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 95 of Werewolf states, under Senses --&gt; Smell<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolves can also identify each other and Wolf-Blooded by smell. Doing so requires a Wits + Primal Urge roll, though this takes an instant action and she has to get in close to the character to be sure. Whether she uses the close press of a nightclub crowd or a tight-knit mob at a riot, she has to invade her suspect\u2019s personal space&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 96 of Werewolf states, under Hishu,<br /> <br /> It's actually what it doesn't state. Despite this being where forms are mechanically defined we don't get a repeat of Hishu's detection immunity. It should really be here if it's a thing.<br /> '<br /> Page 98 of Werewolf states, under Hunter Aspect<br /> <br /> &quot;Uratha know each other at a glance. Apex predators smell their own. This crosses all three of the Uratha\u2019s sensory fields; every single sense can identify one Uratha to another, as the man, the wolf, and the spirit all carry a prominent, forceful aura.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 92 of Blood and Smoke states, in the sidebar &quot;Others and the Predatory Aura&quot; state<br /> <br /> &quot;Other denizens of the World of Darkness may have similar auras. Most well-known is the feral mien of the werewolves. When Kindred notice werewolves, they feel physiological responses they never otherwise experience, such as goose pimples along their arms, and chills down their backs. They feel the adrenaline surge in the pit of the stomach that humans associate with danger and tense excitement.&quot;<br /> <br /> These statements don't line up with each other. I think some of them are in error.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:47:37-08:00","id":430271,"title":"","content":"during chapter 4: rules of the hunt several of the skills have inappropriate specialities listed academics references Theban sorcery, Stealth references Obfuscate and Persuasion references Majesty, while they may be perfectly good specialities for requiem they seem completely out of place and may confuse some new players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:15:09-08:00","id":430292,"title":"","content":"Page 18, in Auspice Benefit. &quot;(the Storyteller might choose to simply allow the action in question <b>or</b> succeed or fail, respectively).&quot;<br /> <br /> The first &quot;or&quot; should be &quot;to&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5253-draeth-darkstar","name":"Draeth Darkstar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:08:41-08:00","id":430382,"title":"","content":"Page 246: &quot;He absently HHswatted at it,&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:55:21-08:00","id":430444,"title":"","content":"p98, 'werewolves set up situations when they can use Strength.' I'm not sure if this is grammatically appropriate. It seems like 'where they can use Strength' would be.<br /> <br /> And on page 95, 'However, the Forsaken are forever denied existing in both places at once, thanks to Father Wolf\u2019s sins.' This might be a change to the mythology, but it seems like it was due to their own sins, not those of Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:08:05-08:00","id":430450,"title":"","content":"On page 245, the Dread Powers of the Mawspawn are in the wrong font and color.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:47:42-08:00","id":430474,"title":"","content":"Question: On page 46 in the Storm Lord section under the First Born heading...why is Skolis-Ur described as the &quot;Oldest Firstborn who bound himself to the Forsaken&quot; and then just below that...All the other first born are already around and sentient before him? Is this just an intentional attempt to play around with the laws of time and age in the shadow? It's not a major issue, just my curiosity and I have a peeve of continuity in time lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:11:20-08:00","id":430482,"title":"","content":"The Facet Ward the Wolf's Den (Glory) uses Cunning to determinate the maximum area warded instead of Glory, pg 135.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:25:39-08:00","id":430508,"title":"","content":"The Influence chart on 187 and the spirit flowchart on 188 reference &quot;Infrastructure&quot; despite there being no explanation of what that is since Angels and the God-Machine are not covered in this rulebook. Might be confusing to people who's first WoD book is this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:49:02-08:00","id":430520,"title":"","content":"Just popping in to say thanks for everyone pointing these out.<br /> <br /> I'll make changes where possible, but we can't do anything that would break the layout. Note specifically that the rules bits included from other books are striped-down to the essentials; as such several human Merits/bits of equipment/Tilts that are in GMC are not present here \u2014 much as VtR2 doesn't include any of the mechanics around Tilts. That they are missing is (almost always) intentional, and 'orphan' references to things that aren't included will be changed as part of fixing errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:49:27-08:00","id":430521,"title":"","content":"Page 164- About Hard Leverage: &quot;If the persuader uses a form of Hard Leverage, it\u2019s a breaking point for him. The Storyteller decides the level of the breaking point. If the difference between that level and the character\u2019s <b>Humanity</b> score is 2 or less, Hard Leverage removes one Door. If the difference is 3 or more, it removes two Doors. Hard Leverage can only be used in conjunction with forcing Doors; remove the Doors before rolling for the character\u2019s approach&quot;<br /> It's obviously copy and paste from Vampire 2e. Thing is Werewolf uses Harmony and it works very different from Humanity. Might be better if it's something closer to the Integrity system in the God-Machine Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:57:29-08:00","id":430639,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 100 and 198: </b>&quot;Tribal bans&quot; are mentioned, but there doesn't seem to be a definition or any other references to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:33:19-08:00","id":430705,"title":"","content":"Page 168 - Hand (\u20134): On a damaging hit, the victim <b>suffersArm</b> Wrack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:33:42-08:00","id":430706,"title":"","content":"Not technically errata, but it seems that starting Renown, Gifts, and Facets works a little differently at character creation than later experience purchases, which has caused some people confusion. Also, as a (possibly unintended?) result of the method used at character creation, doubling up on your Auspice Renown causes you to lose out on a Shadow Gift Facet you would otherwise receive for increasing that Renown later. Bringing starting Shadow Gift Facets up from two to three would solve both problems (though starting characters would be <i>slightly</i> stronger than they are now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:59:15-08:00","id":430742,"title":"","content":"Page 174 - Under Digital Recorder, it's more of a layout problem, the words are really appart like when talkling about Availability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:19:08-08:00","id":430857,"title":"","content":"Under the Evil Eye Tell: &quot;Successive uses of the Evil Eye on a given character suffer a cumulative User to get an e7240 with extra monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.1 penalty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T18:28:29-08:00","id":430957,"title":"","content":"page 187 Mass Create &quot;A spirit can\u2019t permanently alter the mind of a sapient being <b>though</b> Influence.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T20:51:46-08:00","id":430967,"title":"","content":"pg 130: Berserker's Might. &quot;This Facet can be used once per turn as long as the Uratha is in Dalu or Gauru form.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should this Rage facet also be useable in Urshul, or is the restriction to only Dalu and Gauru intentional? It seems strange you can't use it in Urshul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T23:11:39-08:00","id":431082,"title":"","content":"Page 101, 'They can eat the flesh of wolves and humans.' Not werewolves? What happens if you take a chunk out of a werewolf? Page 70 suggests you can eat them. What about vampires and other weird things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-07-2015, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T23:59:05-08:00","id":431124,"title":"","content":"I think at some point, someone's gonna need to consolidate these so people don't double post errata...<br /> <br /> (Not it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T00:47:21-08:00","id":431129,"title":"","content":"Page 106's Embodiment of the Firstborn says, 'When the character spends a point of Willpower, anyone who tries to attack the character that turn gains the Shaken Condition.' This should probably be worded clearer, to see if it's meant to activate when they use a willpower point for anything, or if the ability is meant to activate by directly spending a point of Willpower on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T01:46:34-08:00","id":431142,"title":"","content":"p. 82: &quot;Also, note your character's <b>Instincts</b>, Hunter's Aspect, and Auspice <b>Ability</b>.&quot; There is no capital-I Instinct in the crunch or fluff of character creation and the auspice writeups term each associated unique trick an &quot;Auspice <b>Benefit</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> p.140: &quot;As long as the Uratha keeps the focus about her person, then <b>achieving turns</b> of lucidity during a period of <i>Wasu-Im</i> (not continuous) immediately ends the rage.&quot; Context suggests there should be a number between &quot;achieving&quot; and &quot;turns.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-07-2015, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:24:55-08:00","id":431255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=431142#post431142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> p.140: &quot;As long as the Uratha keeps the focus about her person, then <b>achieving turns</b> of lucidity during a period of <i>Wasu-Im</i> (not continuous) immediately ends the rage.&quot; Context suggests there should be a number between &quot;achieving&quot; and &quot;turns.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's supposed to be 'achieving five turns', iirc from drafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:29:31-08:00","id":431267,"title":"","content":"<b>P. 30:</b> Under the Tactician section, it says &quot;That means setting up the battle after the hunt, and leaving nothing to chance.&quot; Shouldn't it be before the hunt?<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>P. 275:</b> In the section under Poludnica, in the Prey section of Field of Dogs, it says &quot;Notoriously, she is merciless in hunting down those Ithaeur who try to learn her ban through the Warden Moon's Gifts.&quot; Shouldn't that be Crescent Moon's Gifts, since the first facet enables you to learn the ban/bane of a spirit?<br /> <br /> <b>P. 84: </b>In the section on experience point costs, it says rites cost 1 experience. Is that 1 experience per level of the rite?<br /> <br /> Sorry if any of these were already mentioned, but I didn't go through the entire thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","user":"Deranged Goblin","date":". 03-07-2015, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:58:04-08:00","id":431357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deranged Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=431267#post431267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<b>P. 275:</b> In the section under Poludnica, in the Prey section of Field of Dogs, it says &quot;Notoriously, she is merciless in hunting down those Ithaeur who try to learn her ban through the Warden Moon's Gifts.&quot; Shouldn't that be Crescent Moon's Gifts, since the first facet enables you to learn the ban/bane of a spirit?<br /> <br /> <b>P. 84: </b>In the section on experience point costs, it says rites cost 1 experience. Is that 1 experience per level of the rite?<br /> <br /> Sorry if any of these were already mentioned, but I didn't go through the entire thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify in the meantime what the intent is on both these:<br /> <br /> P.275 - the Warden Moon is a reference to Luna, rather than a specific phase. You're correct that the Facet in question is in the Crescent Moon Gift; the sentence is using a slightly more poetic way of saying 'Luna's Gifts'.<br /> <br /> P.84 - Rites cost 1 Experience per dot, yes, so Alliance costs 5 Experiences and Chain Rage costs 1 Experience, for example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:46:10-08:00","id":431663,"title":"","content":"I may have just overlooked it, but outside of the pack creation during chargen, the book doesn't seem to suggest how to get new people into packs. I think it's sort of informal 'you're one of us' type thing, but a sentence to clear it up might be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:41:08-08:00","id":431729,"title":"","content":"Quite a few of the highlighted bits in the screenshots aren't really corrections, more commentary of your style preferences compared with what's in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:10:12-08:00","id":431755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=431663#post431663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have just overlooked it, but outside of the pack creation during chargen, the book doesn't seem to suggest how to get new people into packs. I think it's sort of informal 'you're one of us' type thing, but a sentence to clear it up might be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's up to the characters and the Storyteller. A future book will get closer into how packs work, and how exactly new members join \u2014 and what happens to those who grow disillusioned with their Uratha patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:20:02-08:00","id":431768,"title":"","content":"I think you buy a dot of totem merit and there's a ceremony or something. You introduce yourself to the totem, then there's a welcome party and everyone gets drunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:17:02-08:00","id":431841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>I am uploading a massive amount of corrections in screenshot format via Google Drive for people to look at, I will add more as I read through the book</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>Link deleted</i><br /> <br /> Hopefully someone with correction ability over the final product will find this useful<br /> <br /> edit: removed most comments that could be considered style preferences</div> </div> </div> </div>Please take these down <b>immediately</b>. You've made already made several pages of a <b>brand new book</b> available to absolutely anyone.<br /> <br /> Even if this was not the case, I can't use them. I've<i> already</i> compiled the information in this thread and others into a master list. Having to go through a set of marked-up images to decide which changes I agree with and which is a case of you disagreeing with our house style is work that I do not have time for, especially when I can't copy/paste like I can from a forum post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":28,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","user":"DigitalRaven","date":". 03-07-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:23:49-08:00","id":431847,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't post links to copies of pages from the book. If you've got errors to report, please do so in-thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:34:56-08:00","id":431852,"title":"","content":"You are correct, it was my mistake and I have removed everything. I sincerely apologize for overstepping and all future things found shall be done the traditional way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:14:13-08:00","id":431940,"title":"","content":"Page 93- &quot;As her Primal Urge increases, so do the hardships of a werewolf\u2019s hunt. <b>She cannot hold back the crashing wave<br /> of Kuruth for as long as she once could,</b> as the bloodthirsty predator lurks closer to the surface.&quot;<br /> Extended time in Wasu-Im, before giving in to Kuruth hangs on Harmony not Primal Urge. Primal Urge affects the time in Basu-Im, the more you have, the longer you expend in it, its not about holding back with Primal Urge, it belongs to Harmony.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:32:15-08:00","id":432096,"title":"","content":"Don't know if this has been mentioned, but putting it down to consider.<br /> <br /> Page 165, under &quot;Beat Down and Surrender&quot; section. Second paragraph says, &quot;Before that happens, he can surrender, giving his attacker what she wants according to her intent. If you give in, you gain a point of Willpower and take a Beat, but you take no more part in this fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> The switch from 3rd Person language to 2nd Person language is very confusing. The first sentence is talking about someone else, and the second sentence is talking about you. If you've beat someone down, they can surrender, but YOU have to &quot;give in&quot;? Does this mean if you accept their surrender, you're giving in and you can no longer take part of the fight?<br /> <br /> I dunno. It doesn't read well. Hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:19:15-08:00","id":432135,"title":"","content":"A PDF link error: The Conditions chapter and anything in it links straight back to the cover page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:36:09-08:00","id":432403,"title":"","content":"This may not actually be errata at all, but is it correct that encountering a Kuruth trigger sends you straight into Wasu Im? No roll to resist? That's what the Kuruth section *seems* to be saying, unless I'm just plain missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:58:31-08:00","id":432411,"title":"","content":"This errata isn't actually for the PDF. It's for the 4 page interactive character sheet. Under Auspice abilities on the third page, it has the first edition Auspice abilities listed (Pathfinder's sense for Irraka, Ritualist for Ithaeur, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:32:08-07:00","id":432448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=432403#post432403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may not actually be errata at all, but is it correct that encountering a Kuruth trigger sends you straight into Wasu Im? No roll to resist? That's what the Kuruth section *seems* to be saying, unless I'm just plain missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. Once you encounter a trigger you're fighting for lucidity, either to get away from your friends before you kill them, or to give an Elodoth time to calm you down (or the Chain Rage rite to work).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:38:33-07:00","id":432556,"title":"","content":"Page 217 under Essence Attack<br /> <br /> &quot;The idigam may <u>them</u> consume the Essence itself or allow the spiritual energy to dissipate.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T06:01:05-07:00","id":432566,"title":"","content":"When describing the methods of recovering essence from a locus, it says that &quot;In the Hisil, this means physically touching the locus at its heart. In the physical realms, this means devouring the strange bits of meat and vegetation that appear near the locus.&quot; <br /> <br /> Are these the wrong way round? Only A locus's &quot;heart&quot; is supposed to be a material object and nowhere else does the book mention loci having such drastic effects on their material surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:48:23-07:00","id":432749,"title":"","content":"I noticed that the some Idagm have regeneration, but it does not mention the value from 1 to 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:29:29-07:00","id":432941,"title":"","content":"The text on pages <b>94</b> and <b>95</b> have been transposed with each other, and need to be switched back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:38:45-07:00","id":433053,"title":"","content":"Pg. 301.<br /> <br /> &quot;Boon: Just like the legends say, the Evil Eye can produce<br /> something like a curse if the Wolf-Blooded stares at someone.<br /> Determine a specific action. Spend a point of Willpower and<br /> roll Manipulation + Occult. The victim can resist with Resolve<br /> + Primal Urge. If successful, the next time the victim engages<br /> in that action, it\u2019s automatically a dramatic failure, though the<br /> victim receives a Beat. Successive uses of the Evil Eye on a given<br /> character suffer a cumulative<b> User to get an e7240 with extra<br /> monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.1 penalty.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Unless the curse is that of Advertisement, I think a glitch happened somewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:59:13-07:00","id":433091,"title":"","content":"p185 'as described in the table below' the table is above, on the previous page.<br /> p94 'see the chart on above' should probably lose the 'on'<br /> p168 'the firearms chart (below)' more of a nitpick, the chart is two pages away, perhaps a page number would work better. the firearms chart is on page 170.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:11:33-07:00","id":433112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=433053#post433053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pg. 301.<br /> <br /> &quot;Boon: Just like the legends say, the Evil Eye can produce<br /> something like a curse if the Wolf-Blooded stares at someone.<br /> Determine a specific action. Spend a point of Willpower and<br /> roll Manipulation + Occult. The victim can resist with Resolve<br /> + Primal Urge. If successful, the next time the victim engages<br /> in that action, it\u2019s automatically a dramatic failure, though the<br /> victim receives a Beat. Successive uses of the Evil Eye on a given<br /> character suffer a cumulative<b> User to get an e7240 with extra<br /> monitor from us &amp; run larger jobs on VLX/Condor.1 penalty.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Unless the curse is that of Advertisement, I think a glitch happened somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stew mentioned that this is a copy/paste error. Not at all the spirit of his computer screwing with us/him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:26:36-07:00","id":433119,"title":"","content":"The Immobilized Tilt is not in the book, even though it is referenced. It my need to be included since it is a staple of Uratha Grappling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:52:44-07:00","id":433175,"title":"","content":"The Facet &quot;Pack Triumphs Together&quot; doesn't function as written. You can't take instant actions when rolling initiative, it needs to be Reflexive.<br /> The Facet &quot;Lore of the Land&quot; doesn't have a listed dicepool, despite having a listing for Dramatic Failure / Failure / Success / Exceptional Success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:02:14-07:00","id":433187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=433175#post433175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Facet &quot;Pack Triumphs Together&quot; doesn't function as written. You can't take instant actions when rolling initiative, it needs to be Reflexive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the Instant action should just be for teamwork actions. Should be Reflexive when used for Initiative modification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Facet &quot;Lore of the Land&quot; doesn't have a listed dicepool, despite having a listing for Dramatic Failure / Failure / Success / Exceptional Success. </div> </div> </div>Huh, looks like it got accidentally snipped out of the draft too. Should probably be Int + Survival + Purity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:21:46-07:00","id":433199,"title":"","content":"The Tell &quot;Marked&quot; has no downside to failing the Resolve + Composure roll whilst entering the Marked area. I don;t think that's the intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:35:00-07:00","id":433225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=432448#post432448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's right. Once you encounter a trigger you're fighting for lucidity, either to get away from your friends before you kill them, or to give an Elodoth time to calm you down (or the Chain Rage rite to work).</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks for the clarification Stew. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:01:38-07:00","id":433290,"title":"","content":"Just another nitpick<br /> <br /> In the Breaking Points chart, where it says 'Harmony 3 or lower' and 'Harmony 8 or more' with the dots next to them, like all the other Breaking Points, looks like those in themselves are Breaking Points, which seems weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:28:11-07:00","id":433454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=432749#post432749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that the some Idagm have regeneration, but it does not mention the value from 1 to 5</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about the Regenerate Numen (for instance, the Deceiver Lune has it), it doesn't have a value from 1 to 5. The idigam simply spends Essence and heals accordingly. At least in the version of Regenerate that I have; if it changed in the final version, please disregard (or if I've misinterpreted your comment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:25:10-07:00","id":433541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=433454#post433454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're talking about the Regenerate Numen (for instance, the Deceiver Lune has it), it doesn't have a value from 1 to 5. The idigam simply spends Essence and heals accordingly. At least in the version of Regenerate that I have; if it changed in the final version, please disregard (or if I've misinterpreted your comment).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. It is the Dread Power Regenerate that has a rating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:26:38-07:00","id":433542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 82, Making A Monster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note your character\u2019s <b>Instincts</b>, Hunter\u2019s Aspect, and Auspice Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what I'm missing here. This seems like a leftover from a previous draft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 186, The Shadow And Spirits</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an Uratha has a spirit\u2019s scent, roll Primal Urge minus the spirit\u2019s <b>Resistance</b>. Success reveals the spirit\u2019s highest-rated Influence, while exceptional success reveals them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this supposed to be Resistance and not<i> Rank</i>? It kind of has no real benefit otherwise. Chance dies, chance dies everywhere!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:30:37-07:00","id":433605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=433542#post433542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed to be Resistance and not<i> Rank</i>? It kind of has no real benefit otherwise. Chance dies, chance dies everywhere!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess it's either that, there's a missing second (and possibly third) Trait in the roll, or the roll should be contested rather than resisted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:47:51-07:00","id":433610,"title":"","content":"The character sheet indicates that Gauru form has 1/1 armor, which it does not according to the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:07:31-07:00","id":433621,"title":"","content":"Page 186; The Influence duration chart has durations listed for Influence 0, 1, 2 3, and 4.<br /> <br /> As you can't actually do anything at all with an influence you have no ranks in, I'm guessing these were meant to be 1-5 instead of 0-4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:37:16-07:00","id":433628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/427917-forsaken-2e-errata-thread?p=433621#post433621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 186; The Influence duration chart has durations listed for Influence 0, 1, 2 3, and 4.<br /> <br /> As you can't actually do anything at all with an influence you have no ranks in, I'm guessing these were meant to be 1-5 instead of 0-4.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the way that works is that 0 on the duration chart means you dont need a higher influence to use that rating. The number listed is extra dots of influence needed to enhance th eduration for a given level. So, to strengthen permanently you'd need 5 dots (1 + 4)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:51:26-07:00","id":433634,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>p.88</b> \u201cThe Wilds (Spiritual Touchstone) \u2014 The wilderness calls to your character. Those places where humans </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>dare to tread\u201d</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Should probably be \u201cdare not tread\u201d or \u201cfear to tread\u201d as a think the current wording contradicts the intended meaning.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>p.126</b> \u201cScent the Unnatural will not detect Uratha </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>o</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">r the use of Gifts\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u2018o\u2019 in or isn\u2019t there. Or it is, but the font colour is white and so it can\u2019t be seen in text. At least in my copy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>p.134-135</b> - This isn\u2019t so much errata necessarily as something I worry might be a bit problematic with the Warding Gift as written. The Warding Gift facets for Cunning and for Honor seem like they should be switched. The Honor facet bypasses the need for larceny rolls in lockpicking doors, and seems more like a gift that say, an Irraka or other sneaky type would want to trap a quarry or get into places they otherwise couldn\u2019t. E</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">specially as there's a good chance many Irraka would never get Honor renown, it s</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">eems odd to supplement a non infiltration type Uratha with the means to basically have 100% lockpick power as far as doors are concerned and might overshadow a sneaky type\u2019s utility/purpose in the pack. Whereas the Cunning facet Maze Ward seems more likely to be used for protection as much as escape (especially since it doesn\u2019t affect packmates), and definitely seems more in line with a powerful protector/warden than a trickster/sneaky type. I realize I\u2019m working with some assumptions but I just thought i\u2019d mention it in case the powers that be agreed.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-09-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:16:20-07:00","id":433682,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about this one, but from the context on page 303, Second Skin and Shape Shifted seem to have their forms switched.<br /> Second Skin says that the sibling pelt grants Urshul (Dire Wolf), and the person with the tell feels the urge to run with the pelt. <br /> Shape-Shifted says that it causes a painful transformation into Urhan (regular wolf), and causes Lunacy. The Urhan form does not normally grant Lunacy. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T02:31:55-07:00","id":433732,"title":"","content":"The form is also mentioned to let you regenerate while you're in it, so it can cause lunacy if you heal in front of someone even if it's just urhan. <br /> <br /> Still, why not have both? Two versions of either tell that turn you into one or the other. And maybe one of the involuntary one that turns you dalu instead. No need to make the small slices of werewolf power pie <i>consistent</i> or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:26:17-07:00","id":433878,"title":"","content":"PDF index stuff:<br /> * Elodath is listed twice.<br /> * Numina is a sub heading under Spiritual Influences and Manifestations when it should be its own heading.<br /> * As already noted, Conditions and Tells don't take you to the right page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:00:26-07:00","id":433931,"title":"","content":"Page 262:<br /> <br /> &quot;Belle Isle boasts the only casino in Detroit...&quot;<br /> <br /> There are three casinos in Downtown Detroit: Greektown, MotorCity, and MGM Grand. In fact, the one in Belle Isle Park isn't a gambling facility but is a casino in the old sense of a pavilion or meeting place. That may be what the author meant, but the use of the term here is misleading given the modern understanding of the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:35:58-07:00","id":434299,"title":"","content":"Page 102:<br /> <br /> Death Rage.<br /> <br /> I'd like to suggest adding dice bonuses to the Resolve+Composure to overcome Wasu-Im by directing your rage in Wasu-Im, you smash your mothers favourite chair or your neighbours lamborghini for a +1 or +2 to hit that required exceptional success. Or you carry over bonus dice to your next roll if all you do after succeeding on the Resolve+Composure roll is try to keep your cool.<br /> <br /> I would also like to suggest another option of allowing an extended action Resolve+Composure roll made in non-combat situations that rewards more balanced Harmony Uratha because they actually have time to come down from it, with each roll is one minute of concentrated mental calm down time.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, in my opinion, Wasu-Im is just prolonging dice rolls instead of quicker resolutions for storytelling as you must roll Resolve+Composure to do anything other than attack or damage nearby property, success only buys you turns of control, not minutes, and failure on that roll sends you right into Basu-Im anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-09-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:17:33-07:00","id":434455,"title":"","content":"Maybe each turn you succeed on the roll you can choose to either not do anything violent or or act like you didn't roll at all and bank 